---
metadata: {
    partial_name: "Sign In | Code Hash",
}
---
{%- comment -%}
  The stored form of a sign-in code. Called with:
    function code_hash = 'account/sign_in/code_hash', email: email, code: code
  An HMAC of "email:code" keyed with the SIGN_IN_HMAC_KEY constant, so a code issued to
  one address can never match another address's request, and the table never holds a code.
  Returns blank when the key is not set, and every caller treats blank as a refusal.
  The migration 20261015000000_sign_in_code_hmac_key sets the key.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign code_hash = ''
  assign key = context.constants.SIGN_IN_HMAC_KEY
  if key != blank
    assign message = email | append: ':' | append: code
    assign code_hash = message | compute_hmac: key
  endif
  return code_hash
-%}
